@startuml agent-flow
' Project Vestige agent flow. The rules behind it are in AGENTS.md, "How work is done".
' Render: right-click in VS Code > Preview Current Diagram (PlantUML extension), or
' java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng .claude/agent-flow.puml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #555555
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF4E5
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C98A3A

title Project Vestige: from task to done

start
:**Task picked up**
Main session: roadmap item, David's words;

repeat
  #E8E0F7:**Architect**
  Owner, layer, guide, test plan;
  note right
    Questions for David:
    game feel and design,
    rule changes, licensing,
    money, anything that
    can't be undone
  end note
repeat while (**Design review** by the reviewer) is (changes needed) not (approved)

repeat
  fork
    #DCEBFA:**Implementer**
    Writes the C++, builds clean;
    #DDF3EE:**Test author**
    Tests, build, full suite, PlayTest.md;
  fork again
    #F9E1EC:**Artist** (when art is needed)
    Blender models, import;
  end fork
repeat while (**Code review** by the reviewer\ncode, tests, art, docs) is (changes needed) not (approved)

:**Commit** (main session)
Clean build and full suite after the last change, checklist;
#E2F2DF:**Done**
Report to David lists each technical decision;
stop

legend bottom left
  **Shortcuts**
  Bug fix: the test author writes a failing test first, then the implementer fixes it, then the code review.
  No design choice: skip the architect and the design review.
  Lore, story and typo fixes: no flow.
endlegend
@enduml
